Each program in this portfolio was tested using a combination of valid inputs, invalid inputs, and edge cases to ensure correct behavior and error handling. Below are sample test cases demonstrating how the programs were verified.

Input Final Analyst Program:
| Test Case | Input | Expected Output | Actual Output | Notes |
| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
| Valid input | Numeric values | Correct final analysis summary | Correct | No issues |
| Invalid input | Letters or symbols | Error message or reprompt | Reprompt displayed | Input validation works |
| Edge case | Very large numbers | Proper handling without crash | Correct | Stable under large values |

Shapes Program
Test Case	Input	Expected Output	Actual Output	Notes
Valid shape choice	Square, triangle, etc.	Correct shape printed	Correct	Output matches assignment
Invalid shape	Unknown shape name	Error message	Error displayed	Works as expected
Edge case	Empty input	Reprompt	Reprompt	Good validation

Tank AI Program
Test Case	Input	Expected Output	Actual Output	Notes
